### Normalized scores (1–100)

**Tool use: 90/100.** No direct public benchmark scores. Estimated based on rank #8/214 on AI Intelligence Index and similar-tier models' performance. Caps: top-10 performance among reasoning models at ~$2-10/M pricing.

**Reasoning: 92/100.** Artificial Analysis Intelligence Index: 53 (rank #8/214). GDPval-AA and HLE benchmarks not publicly scored. Comparison: similar-tier models (e.g., Claude Opus 5.5: 58, GPT-6 Astra: ~54). Caps: strong reasoning, but not top-of-class; below Claude Opus 5.5.

**Context window: 100/100.** 1M tokens measured. Caps: highest among evaluated models at this tier; enables longest document processing and complex RAG.

**Multimodal: 100/100.** Text + image input, text output. 1M context supports long documents and image analysis. Caps: standard full multimodal for frontier models.

**Coding: 88/100.** No direct public coding benchmarks. Estimated based on Intelligence Index composite score and similar-tier models. Caps: strong but unproven coding; lacks terminal/coding-specific benchmarks.

**Cost efficiency: 80/100.** $2/M input, $10/M output. $1.99 per Intelligence Index task. Cache discount: 95%. 82.2 tokens/s. Verbose: 110M tokens from Intelligence Index (rank #77/115). Caps: excellent value among frontier models; competitive cost-efficiency.

**Overall Score: 92/100.** Mean of Tool (90) + Reasoning (92) + Context (100) + Multimodal (100) + Coding (88) = 95.2. High-performance reasoning model with strong cost-efficiency; lacks detailed coding benchmark data.

